{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>To freedom he shall send him.</b> The slave has no right to take money in place of his tooth and his eye, for what good would it do him, since whatever a slave acquires his master acquires? And even if he sold himself on condition that his master has no authority over him, the master can press him in various ways until he gives him the money against his will. Therefore his only remedy is freedom."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:59:31.016358736Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}